The shuru-screen binary links x264 (https://www.videolan.org/developers/x264.html),
which is under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. The
binary is therefore a combined work and is distributed under the terms of
the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. Its complete source is
this crate, in the public shuru repository:

    https://github.com/superhq-ai/shuru/tree/main/crates/shuru-screen

The binary links x264 and libyuv dynamically, from the system (the Debian
packages libx264 and libyuv). No other shuru crate links x264: programs
talk to shuru-screen over its unix socket.

patches/xorg-server-xtest-scroll.patch is a change to xorg-server
(Xext/xtest.c), from voxl under the MIT license. xorg-server is under the
X11 license; an Xvfb built with the patch is distributed under that
license, with the license header of the patched file kept as it is.
